# Channel Engine Service Configuration
# Copy this file to .env and update values for your environment

# ============================================================
# CHANNEL_ENGINE_PATH (Required for production)
# ============================================================
# Absolute path to a local ChannelEgine clone (NOT a GitHub URL).
# Must include Phase 1+ of the strict-PFS rollout (PR #1 onward in
# the ChannelEgine repo); older clones missing MIMO_OTA_Simulator
# will fail startup validation.
#
# Setup:
#   git clone https://github.com/swang430/ChannelEgine.git /path/to/ChannelEgine
#   CHANNEL_ENGINE_PATH=/path/to/ChannelEgine
#
# Examples:
#   macOS:   /Users/yourname/Tools/ChannelEgine
#   Linux:   /home/yourname/ChannelEgine
#   Windows: C:\Users\yourname\ChannelEgine
#
# As of 2026-05-18 (P0-7): if this path is unset / missing /
# doesn't expose `mimo_ota_simulator.simulator.MIMO_OTA_Simulator`,
# the service FAILS TO START. Previous behavior (silent fallback
# to mock placeholder .asc) caused production fake-data incidents.
#
CHANNEL_ENGINE_PATH=/path/to/your/local/ChannelEgine

# ============================================================
# MOCK_ASC_MODE (Debug only — DO NOT SET IN PRODUCTION)
# ============================================================
# When set to "1" / "true" / "yes":
#   - Startup skips the CHANNEL_ENGINE_PATH validation above.
#   - All synthesize_hardware_pipeline requests return placeholder
#     .asc (1-tap Doppler shift, NOT real PFS synthesis) with
#     `mock_mode: true` in the response body.
# Intended use: local dev iteration on endpoint shape without
# requiring a ChannelEgine clone. Strictly forbidden in any
# environment that talks to a real F64 or to operators.
#
# MOCK_ASC_MODE=1

# ============================================================
# Server configuration (Optional)
# ============================================================
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# PORT=8001
